planner finding (zero-join path; resolved by AliasRoot, NOT a DO->PLAN blocker):
  QueryPlanner.GetFrom(Type srcType, QueryCommand? queryCommand) unwraps `Item1` (mapping the projection's
  root to the underlying entity) ONLY when `queryCommand.Joins?.Length > 0`. For a zero-join root
  projection the projection type is not a registered entity, so the unwrap branch is skipped and
  `GetFrom(projectionType)` throws BuildSqlCommandException ("Table name is not registered for type ...").
  Resolution: AliasRoot materializes the mapped root's explicit FromExpression once into
  `rooted.SourceFrom` (`_dataProvider.GetFrom(_sourceEntityType ?? typeof(TEntity), null)`), so the
  zero-join planner path uses the physical source and renders `select Id from orders`. No planner edit is
  required. This closes the D:160-02 success criterion; CHECK should treat it as resolved-by-AliasRoot.

